# Vite's dev server restricts which files a browser may read through the
# `server.fs` allow list: `viteServeRawFsMiddleware`
# (packages/vite/src/node/server/middlewares/static.ts) takes `/@fs/`-prefixed
# request URLs, decodes the pathname and hands it to sirv, whose `shouldServe`
# consults `checkLoadingAccess` -> `isFileLoadingAllowed`. That checker is a
# pure string decision:
#
#   if (config.fsDenyGlob(filePathWithoutTrailingSlash)) return false
#   if (config.safeModulePaths.has(filePath)) return true
#   if (fs.allow.some((uri) => isUriInFilePath(uri, filePath))) return true
#   return false
#
# On Windows two spellings of a path name the same file while comparing as
# different strings: 8.3 short names (`DOTENV~1` for `.env`) and NTFS
# alternate data streams (`.env:hidden`, `file.html::$DATA`). A request for
# `/@fs/C:/.../DOTENV~1` or `/@fs/.../.env:hidden` clears the deny glob and
# the allow-list prefix comparison as a literal string, and the filesystem
# then resolves it to the denied file, which is served. The fixed revision inserts two
# early rejections into the checker itself -- a path containing `~` on
# Windows, and a `:` anywhere after the drive letter -- so no alternate
# spelling survives the string comparison.
#
# The decisive property of this fix, measured: it touches nothing but
# `isFileLoadingAllowed`'s own body (plus playground tests/config). Every
# caller -- `viteServeRawFsMiddleware`, sirv's `shouldServe`,
# `transformMiddleware`, `indexHtml` -- is byte-identical across the two
# revisions, so no caller-anchored binding can separate them, and a binding
# anchored inside the checker would have to negate on `includes('~')` /
# `includes(':')` -- the fixing commit's own vocabulary, absent from any
# library documentation (the genericity test fails on its face). The 1380
# counterweight does not apply: the fixed revision leaves no API-documented call inside
# the function it guards, only `.includes`/`.test`/`.slice` string builtins
# on the same variable.
#
# Measured, bounded subtree scan of packages/vite/src/node (the change touches
# no source outside it), three `--cache off` runs per revision, timeout 180,
# --max-ram 6GB: a byte-stable 521 findings at the fixed revision's parent AND
# at the fix, 252 at or above high on both (110 SEC-001, 92 INJ-001, 67
# PATH-001, 62 INJ-013, 51 INJ-009, 35 INJ-002, ...). The rule multiset and
# the per-file multiset are identical across the two revisions; static.ts
# carries five sink rows on both (INJ-011 :164, INJ-004 :182/:220, INJ-009 and
# SEC-001 :332), and the only positional change is the two rows below the
# inserted block moving 332 -> 347. The PATH-001 sinks sit in optimizer/,
# plugins/ and utils.ts (optimizer/index.ts 12, plugins/css.ts 6, utils.ts 6,
# ssr/runtime tests 5, ...), none on the raw-fs middleware. A `-flags only`
# run is identical too: 72 flags on both revisions, the two on static.ts
# being core.PathAccessCheck on `checkLoadingAccess` (:63) and on
# `utils.isParentDirectory` (:266).
#
# Where detection actually stops, pinned by the third and fourth cases as a
# minimal pair: the request URL source and the decodeURI plumbing are fully
# labelled (`req.url` -> code.HttpInput, including the middleware's own reads
# at :214/:215), and with a direct `fs.readFile` on the decoded path
# VYQL-PATH-001 fires -- but only without the guard. `trace -brief` on the
# file reports six reachable source->sink pairs and twenty-five dead-end
# sources, none of them a file read; `explain` shows two proof trees, both on
# the log and html-render sinks. Two independent walls stand in front of the
# real flow:
#   1. the read happens inside sirv, a dependency whose source is not in the
#      tree: `serveFromRoot(req, res, next)` carries the request object, not
#      the decoded path, and no binding names sirv at all -- a sirv sink
#      would see no request data either, because the options handed to the
#      factory close over `config`, not over the request;
#   2. `checkLoadingAccess` is bound as core.PathAccessCheck
#      (pathAccessCheck526), so even a direct read behind the guard is
#      suppressed -- in both revisions, since the guard exists unchanged in
#      both. The vulnerability is precisely that the guard's string
#      comparisons admit an alternate spelling of the same file, and no
#      taint relation can see inside them. The rejections the fix adds land
#      as `vyql.internal.NeutralizerAssumption` (`filePath.includes` :279 and
#      `?.includes` :286 on the fixed tree), not as any control concept, so
#      they neither suppress a flow nor signal one on their own.
#
# Reuse is checked before concluding ATTENTION: the concept
# code.MiddlewarePathMatchNormalizationMismatch (VYQL-AUTH-127, CWE-863/436)
# states this weakness class exactly -- "the path it matches, opens or looks
# up is not the path that decision is taken from" -- but both its shipped
# bindings key on a decoder (decodeURIComponent) or a router-vs-handler
# normalization mismatch, neither of which exists here: vite decodes with
# decodeURI, which correctly leaves reserved delimiters encoded, and the
# decision and the open use the same string. Reaching the concept from this
# code needs the negation on the `~`/`:` checks, i.e. the fixed revision itself. This
# is the URL-allowlist-bypass family (a string allow/deny decision defeated
# by an alternate representation of the same resource) and the
# callee-centralised-fix shape (a caller-side label cannot discriminate),
# both measured unshippable.
#
# All cases assert reject VYQL-PATH-001 and reject VYQL-AUTH-127 except the
# third, which pins the plumbing with expect VYQL-PATH-001. If an
# alternate-path-representation rule ever ships (keyed on a path checked by
# string membership and then opened, without rejecting the filesystem's
# short-name and stream spellings), the first case -- the vulnerable checker
# form -- is the one that must flip to expect; the second (patched checker)
# and fourth (guard present) must stay reject.

test "rank1920: the raw-fs middleware decodes the request path into a sirv-served file the allow list cleared as a literal string"
  lang javascript
  file static.ts
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-127
  code
  ```
  declare const config: any
  declare const isWindows: boolean
  const FS_PREFIX = '/@fs/'

  export function isFileLoadingAllowed(config: any, filePath: string): boolean {
    const { fs } = config.server

    if (!fs.strict) return true

    const filePathWithoutTrailingSlash = filePath.endsWith('/')
      ? filePath.slice(0, -1)
      : filePath
    if (config.fsDenyGlob(filePathWithoutTrailingSlash)) return false

    if (config.safeModulePaths.has(filePath)) return true

    if (fs.allow.some((uri: string) => isUriInFilePath(uri, filePath))) return true

    return false
  }

  declare function isUriInFilePath(uri: string, filePath: string): boolean

  export function checkLoadingAccess(
    config: any,
    path: string,
  ): 'allowed' | 'denied' | 'fallback' {
    if (isFileLoadingAllowed(config, path)) {
      return 'allowed'
    }
    return 'denied'
  }

  export function viteServeRawFsMiddleware(req: any, res: any, next: any) {
    const serveFromRoot = sirv('/', {
      dev: true,
      etag: true,
      shouldServe: (filePath: string) => {
        const servingAccessResult = checkLoadingAccess(config, filePath)
        return servingAccessResult === 'allowed'
      },
    })

    if (req.url!.startsWith(FS_PREFIX)) {
      const url = new URL(req.url!, 'http://example.com')
      const pathname = decodeURI(url.pathname)
      let newPathname = pathname.slice(FS_PREFIX.length)
      if (isWindows) newPathname = newPathname.replace(/^[A-Z]:/i, '')
      url.pathname = encodeURI(newPathname)
      req.url = url.href.slice(url.origin.length)

      serveFromRoot(req, res, next)
    } else {
      next()
    }
  }

  declare function sirv(dir: string, opts: any): any
  ```

test "rank1920: the checker that rejects windows short names and stream suffixes is indistinguishable by anything but its own string tests"
  lang javascript
  file static-patched.ts
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  reject VYQL-AUTH-127
  code
  ```
  declare const config: any
  declare const isWindows: boolean
  const FS_PREFIX = '/@fs/'
  const windowsDriveRE = /^[A-Z]:/i

  export function isFileLoadingAllowed(config: any, filePath: string): boolean {
    const { fs } = config.server

    if (!fs.strict) return true

    if (isWindows && filePath.includes('~')) {
      // `~` is used for Windows 8.3 short names, which can be used to bypass the check.
      return false
    }

    const hasDriveLetter = isWindows && windowsDriveRE.test(filePath)
    const hasColon = (hasDriveLetter ? filePath.slice(2) : filePath).includes(':')
    if (hasColon) {
      // the `:` is included in the path which may be used for NTFS ADS
      return false
    }

    const filePathWithoutTrailingSlash = filePath.endsWith('/')
      ? filePath.slice(0, -1)
      : filePath
    if (config.fsDenyGlob(filePathWithoutTrailingSlash)) return false

    if (config.safeModulePaths.has(filePath)) return true

    if (fs.allow.some((uri: string) => isUriInFilePath(uri, filePath))) return true

    return false
  }

  declare function isUriInFilePath(uri: string, filePath: string): boolean

  export function checkLoadingAccess(
    config: any,
    path: string,
  ): 'allowed' | 'denied' | 'fallback' {
    if (isFileLoadingAllowed(config, path)) {
      return 'allowed'
    }
    return 'denied'
  }

  export function viteServeRawFsMiddleware(req: any, res: any, next: any) {
    const serveFromRoot = sirv('/', {
      dev: true,
      etag: true,
      shouldServe: (filePath: string) => {
        const servingAccessResult = checkLoadingAccess(config, filePath)
        return servingAccessResult === 'allowed'
      },
    })

    if (req.url!.startsWith(FS_PREFIX)) {
      const url = new URL(req.url!, 'http://example.com')
      const pathname = decodeURI(url.pathname)
      let newPathname = pathname.slice(FS_PREFIX.length)
      if (isWindows) newPathname = newPathname.replace(/^[A-Z]:/i, '')
      url.pathname = encodeURI(newPathname)
      req.url = url.href.slice(url.origin.length)

      serveFromRoot(req, res, next)
    } else {
      next()
    }
  }

  declare function sirv(dir: string, opts: any): any
  ```

test "rank1920: the same decoded request path read directly with no guard reports the traversal"
  lang javascript
  file direct-read.ts
  expect VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  declare const fs: { readFile(p: string, cb: (e: any, d: any) => void): void }
  const FS_PREFIX = '/@fs/'

  export function serveFromFs(req: any, res: any, next: any) {
    if (req.url!.startsWith(FS_PREFIX)) {
      const url = new URL(req.url!, 'http://example.com')
      const pathname = decodeURI(url.pathname)
      let newPathname = pathname.slice(FS_PREFIX.length)
      url.pathname = encodeURI(newPathname)
      req.url = url.href.slice(url.origin.length)
      fs.readFile(newPathname, (err, data) => {
        res.end(data)
      })
    } else {
      next()
    }
  }
  ```

test "rank1920: a direct read behind the allow-list guard is suppressed on both revisions of the guard"
  lang javascript
  file guarded-read.ts
  reject VYQL-PATH-001
  code
  ```
  declare const fs: { readFile(p: string, cb: (e: any, d: any) => void): void }
  declare const config: any
  const FS_PREFIX = '/@fs/'

  export function isFileLoadingAllowed(config: any, filePath: string): boolean {
    const { fs } = config.server
    if (!fs.strict) return true
    const filePathWithoutTrailingSlash = filePath.endsWith('/')
      ? filePath.slice(0, -1)
      : filePath
    if (config.fsDenyGlob(filePathWithoutTrailingSlash)) return false
    if (config.safeModulePaths.has(filePath)) return true
    if (fs.allow.some((uri: string) => isUriInFilePath(uri, filePath))) return true
    return false
  }

  declare function isUriInFilePath(uri: string, filePath: string): boolean

  export function checkLoadingAccess(
    config: any,
    path: string,
  ): 'allowed' | 'denied' | 'fallback' {
    if (isFileLoadingAllowed(config, path)) {
      return 'allowed'
    }
    return 'denied'
  }

  export function serveFromFs(req: any, res: any, next: any) {
    if (req.url!.startsWith(FS_PREFIX)) {
      const url = new URL(req.url!, 'http://example.com')
      const pathname = decodeURI(url.pathname)
      const filePath = pathname.slice(FS_PREFIX.length)
      if (checkLoadingAccess(config, filePath) === 'allowed') {
        fs.readFile(filePath, (err, data) => {
          res.end(data)
        })
        return
      }
      res.statusCode = 403
      res.end('denied')
    } else {
      next()
    }
  }
  ```
